      Desc="We could use a grayscale texture to distort the entire volume density, vertically.\r\nExample 1 - we could make our volume perfectly align with the ground surface,\r\nby sampling landscape elevation and use the data as heightmap for the volume\r\nExample 2 - we could make a cone from a flat volume, by using a radial gradient as heightmap\r\nExample 3 - we could use a top-down scenecapture camera to get scene depth,\r\nand make the volume creep upon object surfaces"
   End Object
